# Code placement

When adding or moving files, read [ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) and place code by concern.

## Folders (main)

- `app` — Electron lifecycle / window only
- `ipc` — thin handlers; no scrape / heavy SQL
- `browser` + `browser/auth/<platform>.ts` — Playwright, human gate, per-platform login
- `scrape` — orchestration + URL parse; platform work in `scrape/<platform>/`
- `db` — schema + model types (not queries)
- `code` — SQLite read/write
- `core` — connect, paths, migrate
- `products` — list/get/update, gallery, on-disk folders
- `media` — `ml-media://`
- `jobs` — job logs
- Shared IPC types → `src/shared/types`

Do not invent a new `src/main/` top-level folder without a real new concern.

## Marketplaces

- After platform is known, branch immediately. Routers (`marketAuth.ts`, `scrape/product.ts`) only dispatch.
- Temu and AliExpress stay in **separate** folders/files. Duplicate over shared — no shared fetch/parsers for both.
- Future merge decision: [docs/features-later.md](docs/features-later.md). Do not consolidate platforms early.

## File size

- One step/type per file; soft cap ~200–250 lines. Thin IPC.
